  "body": "Some homes offer a beautiful place to live. Others offer an entire way of life.\r\n\r\nExperience the seamless flow and light-filled interiors through the VIDEO TOUR, and explore the home from every perspective via the interactive 3D VIRTUAL TOUR, accessed through the box icon.\r\n\r\nSet within one of Devonport's most sought-after coastal neighbourhoods, this gracious villa enjoys a rare connection to the beaches, waterfront and village that define this much-loved seaside community.\r\n\r\nCheltenham and Torpedo Bay beaches are moments away, while North Head provides a spectacular backdrop to morning walks and weekend adventures. The waterfront leads naturally towards the village, where cafes, restaurants, boutiques and the celebrated ferry connection to Auckland CBD are all within easy reach.\r\n\r\nIt is a setting that quietly shapes the rhythm of everyday life. A morning swim at the beach, a walk along the waterfront, coffee in the village, an afternoon outdoors, then home to the privacy of your own garden. Here, the pleasures of coastal living are not reserved for weekends; they become part of the everyday.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of the property is a villa dating to the early 1900s, offering the generous proportions, character and sense of permanence that make homes of this era so enduringly appealing. Across 150sqm, this residence provides three bedrooms, two bathrooms, two living areas, secure garaging and off-street parking, positioned on a 465sqm freehold site.\r\n\r\nThere is an authenticity to a home with this kind of history that cannot easily be recreated. Its proportions and character provide a compelling foundation, while the existing spaces offer scope to further enhance and refine the home for contemporary living.\r\n\r\nFor its next owner, there is the opportunity to introduce a personal aesthetic and bring your own personality to the property, respecting its architectural character while shaping the interiors and surroundings to reflect the way you want to live.\r\n\r\nThe scale of the site adds another layer of appeal, with space to enjoy the garden, entertain, relax and allow family life to unfold. Whether imagined as a much-loved family home, a coastal retreat or a long-term investment in one of Auckland's most tightly held village environments, the foundations are compelling.\r\n\r\nWhat makes this opportunity particularly appealing is the balance between what is already here and what could become.\r\n\r\nA home with history, but not defined by it.\r\nA setting with enduring appeal, but never standing still.\r\nA property with character, substance and the freedom to make it distinctly your own.\r\n\r\nMore than simply a character home in a desirable location, this is an opportunity to become part of the enduring rhythm of Devonport; a place where the beach, village, waterfront and community are woven naturally into daily life.\r\n\r\nA timeless setting.\r\nA home of genuine character.\r\nAnd the opportunity to create something that feels entirely your own.\r\n\r\nFor those seeking a coastal lifestyle with substance, space and the freedom to shape what comes next, this is a rare opportunity to secure a piece of classic blue-chip Devonport and make it your own.\r\n\r\nProudly marketed by The EK Group, delivering prestige, passion, and property without parallel.",
